EXPERIMENT 8
Normalization in Oracle (1NF, 2NF, 3NF, 4NF, 5NF) using Functional Dependencies

AIM
To study and implement Normalization (1NF, 2NF, 3NF, 4NF, 5NF) using Functional Dependencies, and to design and create normalized tables in Oracle using SQL.

THEORY
Normalization organizes data to reduce redundancy and avoid insertion, update, and deletion anomalies. Functional Dependency X → Y means each value of X determines exactly one value of Y.
• 1NF: atomic values; no repeating groups.
• 2NF: 1NF and no partial dependency.
• 3NF: 2NF and no transitive dependency.
• BCNF: every determinant is a candidate key.
• 4NF: BCNF and no multivalued dependency.
• 5NF/PJNF: 4NF and no non-key join dependency.

PROCEDURE
Analyze the unnormalized StudentCourse relation and decompose it step by step, creating and populating the normalized Oracle tables.

RESULT
The manual demonstrates decomposition through 1NF, 2NF, 3NF, 4NF, and 5NF using functional-dependency analysis.

